{"reference":"Zechariah 13","book":"Zechariah","chapter":13,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the Chapter as a Whole","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter places cleansing, the removal of idols and deceptive prophecy, the striking of a shepherd, and the testing of a surviving third within one oracle. It begins with a fountain opened for the house of David and Jerusalem to address sin and impurity. It then describes a community in which false prophetic claims are rejected, before turning to scattered sheep after the shepherd is struck. The final image is not merely survival: the remaining third is refined and tested, calls on YHWH’s name, and is answered in renewed mutual recognition.","verse_refs":["Zechariah 13:1-6","Zechariah 13:7","Zechariah 13:8-9"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_zechariah_013_95d85f9d5e362d9c67f323e8"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}